## Query: "site:docs.sentry.io/platforms/javascript/guides/cloudflare/ Cloudflare Workers withSentry beforeSend worker error reporting"

Use `@sentry/cloudflare` and wrap the Worker’s ESM handler with `Sentry.withSentry`. Configure `beforeSend` in the per-`env` options callback; return `null` to discard noisy events. The package currently exports both `withSentry` and `captureException`. ([github.com](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/blob/develop/packages/cloudflare/README.md))

```ts
import * as Sentry from "@sentry/cloudflare";

type Env = { SENTRY_DSN: string };

export default Sentry.withSentry(
  (env: Env) => ({
    dsn: env.SENTRY_DSN,

    beforeSend(event, hint) {
      const error = hint.originalException;

      // Drop expected/noisy errors.
      if (error instanceof Error && error.message.includes("ExpectedError")) {
        return null;
      }

      // Avoid placing secrets, auth headers, or raw PII in event data.
      event.tags = { ...event.tags, runtime: "cloudflare-worker" };
      return event;
    },
  }),
  {
    async fetch(request, env, ctx) {
      try {
        // Worker logic
        throw new Error("Example worker failure");
      } catch (error) {
        Sentry.captureException(error);
        return new Response("Internal Server Error", { status: 500 });
      }
    },
  } satisfies ExportedHandler<Env>,
);
```

Install with `npm install @sentry/cloudflare`. For a Worker compatibility date **before August 4, 2026**, add `nodejs_compat`; Cloudflare enables it by default for dates on or after that date. ([github.com](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/blob/develop/packages/cloudflare/README.md))

```toml
# wrangler.toml
compatibility_flags = ["nodejs_compat"]
```

For current Sentry v11-style Cloudflare configuration, `nodejs_compat` is the required compatibility mode, replacing the prior `nodejs_als` requirement. ([github.com](https://github.com/getsentry/sentry-javascript/blob/develop/MIGRATION.md?utm_source=openai))

