## Query: "site:developers.cloudflare.com/workers/observability/ logs traces metrics worker observability configuration"

Cloudflare Workers observability has three main layers:

- **Logs:** Enable Workers Logs in Wrangler; it captures invocation logs, `console.*` output, errors, and uncaught exceptions. Control volume with `head_sampling_rate` from `0` to `1` (default `1`). ([developers.cloudflare.com](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/observability/logs/workers-logs/?utm_source=openai))
- **Traces:** Workers provides automatic instrumentation for handler invocations, `fetch`, and bindings such as KV, R2, and Durable Objects—no SDK or code changes required. Enable custom/trace collection explicitly under `observability.traces.enabled`. ([developers.cloudflare.com](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/observability/?utm_source=openai))
- **Metrics:** Built-in Worker metrics cover requests, successes/errors, subrequests, CPU time, wall time, and execution duration. For application-specific metrics such as signups or per-customer usage, use Analytics Engine. ([developers.cloudflare.com](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/observability/metrics-and-analytics/?utm_source=openai))

Example `wrangler.jsonc` configuration:

```jsonc
{
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true,
    "logs": {
      "enabled": true,
      "invocation_logs": true,
      "head_sampling_rate": 0.1
    },
    "traces": {
      "enabled": true,
      "head_sampling_rate": 0.05
    }
  }
}
```

For external tooling, Cloudflare can export **logs and traces** to OTLP-compatible destinations; Worker and custom metrics cannot currently be exported via this integration. ([developers.cloudflare.com](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/observability/exporting-opentelemetry-data/?utm_source=openai))

Use the dashboard’s **Query Builder** or Observability REST API to filter, group, and visualize stored Workers Logs. ([developers.cloudflare.com](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/observability/query-builder/?utm_source=openai))

