## Query: "site:docs.sentry.io/platforms/javascript/guides/cloudflare/ privacy sendDefaultPii request headers scrub beforeSend"

For **Sentry’s Cloudflare JavaScript SDK**, keep `sendDefaultPii` disabled unless you explicitly need PII. Use `beforeSend` to strip sensitive request headers client-side **before events leave the Worker**, and also enable Sentry’s server-side data scrubbing as defense in depth. Sentry supports default and custom sensitive-field scrubbers plus advanced PII rules applied before storage. ([docs.sentry.io](https://docs.sentry.io/api/organizations/update-an-organization/?utm_source=openai))

```ts
Sentry.init({
  dsn: env.SENTRY_DSN,
  sendDefaultPii: false,

  beforeSend(event) {
    const headers = event.request?.headers;

    if (headers) {
      for (const key of Object.keys(headers)) {
        if (/^(authorization|cookie|set-cookie|x-api-key)$/i.test(key)) {
          delete headers[key];
        }
      }
    }

    // Optional: remove other potentially sensitive request data
    delete event.request?.data;
    delete event.user?.email;
    delete event.user?.ip_address;

    return event;
  },
});
```

`beforeSend` is the appropriate final client-side event hook for filtering or modifying outbound event content; Sentry’s docs also recommend client-side filtering with `beforeSend` alongside server-side controls. ([docs.sentry.io](https://docs.sentry.io/pdfs/developer-quick-reference-guide.pdf?utm_source=openai))

Separately, do not confuse request-header scrubbing with tracing headers: for cross-origin tracing, Cloudflare/backend CORS may need to allow `sentry-trace` and `baggage`; these are tracing-propagation headers, not credentials. ([docs.sentry.io](https://docs.sentry.io/platforms/javascript/guides/cloudflare/tracing/trace-propagation/dealing-with-cors-issues/?utm_source=openai))

